<title>USA: Cargill says N. Korea grain negotiations ongoing.</title>
<headline>Cargill says N. Korea grain negotiations ongoing.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargill Inc Wednesday said talks with North Korea to arrange financing for grain purchases were ongoing and it was hopeful an agreement will be reached.</p>
<p>&quot;We are still in negotiations and we're optimistic that we will be able to reach some kind of agreement,&quot; said Cargill spokesperson Lori Johnson.</p>
<p>&quot;I don't know what timeframe is a reasonable timeframe to expect that agreement to be completed however,&quot; Johnson added.</p>
<p>Cargill has been negotiating with North Korea since the beginning of this year to work out a deal to sell 500,000 tonnes wheat and/or rice to the communist nation.</p>
<p>North Korea reportedly asked for financing from the U.S. government -- which Washington said it would not provide for the commercial deal -- and Cargill reportedly is trying to work out some sort of barter arrangement with North Korea.</p>
